---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Sakina, a software engineer building CLI tools, browser extensions, and Minecraft mods.">
  <section class="page-intro narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm Sakina.</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a programmer who likes building fast, practical command-line tools, browser extensions, and Minecraft mods.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose narrow">
    <p>
      Most of my open-source repositories start because I got tired of clicking through a slow web UI or maintaining a brittle one-off script. Lately that has meant <a href="https://github.com/soffits/ikea-cli">ikea-cli</a>, <a href="https://github.com/soffits/bookfetch-cli">bookfetch-cli</a>, <a href="https://github.com/soffits/seafile-vault-cli">seafile-vault-cli</a>, <a href="https://github.com/soffits/canvas-student-cli">canvas-student-cli</a>, <a href="https://github.com/soffits/jobloom">jobloom</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/soffits/OpenPlayer">OpenPlayer</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a bug takes an unexpected turn—an Auth0 error page returning HTTP 200, a hover button sliding out from under the cursor, or `tailscale0` losing its routing table on OpenWrt—I write up the diagnosis and the fix here so I have it next time (and in case someone else searches the same error line).
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
